hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2928","\n Narrated to us by Abu al-Khattab, Ziyad bin Yahya, who said: Narrated to us by Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik (RA), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had thrown the pebbles at the Jamrah and sacrificed his Hadi"","" he handed over the right half of his head to the barber"","" who shaved it. Then he handed over the left half to Abu Tal"""""
